entry.summary:
So, you want to make a game? Python and JavaScript are a great combo for getting started, especially if you're a beginner. Python is fantastic for handling the game's logic and backend, while JavaScript is perfect for the frontend—what players actually see and interact with. Let's walk through how you can create a simple text-based guessing game. Part 1: Setting Up with Python We'll start with Python. The game's core logic will be a simple "guess the number" game. The computer will pick a random number, and the player will try to guess it. Here's the Python code for our game's backend. You can save this as game_logic.py. import random
def generate_random_number(): """Generates a random number between 1 and 100.""" return random.randint(1, 100)
